$\begin{align}
3x^2&=xy
\\\\
6x\cdot\dfrac{dx}{dt}&=y\cdot\dfrac{dx}{dt}+x\cdot\dfrac{dy}{dt}
\end{align}$

We are given that $\goldD{\dfrac{dy}{dt}=-3}$, and we want to find $\dfrac{dx}{dt}$ when $\blueD{x=-6}$.

We also need to find the corresponding value of $\maroonD{y}$. To do that, we can plug $\blueD{x=-6}$ into the relating equation:

$\begin{align}
3\blueD{x}^2&=\blueD{x}\maroonD{y}
\\\\
3(\blueD{-6})^2&=(\blueD{-6})\maroonD{y}
\\\\
108&=-6\maroonD{y}
\\\\
\maroonD{-18}&\maroonD{=y}
\end{align}$
